## Summary

Closes #605.

The live inspection model already exposed detailed health-probe and schema-watch state, but the static HTML dashboard discarded most of it. This PR closes that model-to-UI gap without changing execution or routing semantics.

### Changes
- render health monitor state plus every registered health probe;
- show access path, probe status, current runtime availability, last check, and safe error type;
- visually mark access paths in the bounded unavailable cooldown;
- render schema watcher state plus every registered watch;
- show interval, last check/apply timestamps, compatibility, pending-review state/change count, and safe error type;
- visually mark pending-review/error/stale schema-watch rows;
- preserve the existing privacy boundary: no credentials, payloads, raw exceptions, or arbitrary metadata are rendered;
- add focused regression coverage for healthy/unavailable/unknown probes and applied/pending/error schema-watch states.

## Scope

Dashboard/inspection presentation only. No frozen 0.14 research semantics, route selection, execution authority, schema-refresh behavior, or registry contracts are changed.

